"Positive Lyapunov Exponent in the Hopf Normal Form with Additive Noise (https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.06547)\nciteturn7academia12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.9 years ago; Title: Positive Lyapunov Exponent in the Hopf Normal Form with Additive Noise\nAuthors: Dennis Chemnitz, Maximilian Engel\nTitle: Positive Lyapunov Exponent in the Hopf Normal Form with Additive Noise\nAuthors: Dennis Chemnitz, Maximilian Engel\nDate: Tue Dec 13 12:59:33 2022\n\nWe prove the positivity of Lyapunov exponents for the normal form of a Hopf bifurcation, perturbed by additive white noise, under sufficiently strong shear strength. This completes a series of related results for simplified situations which we can exploit by studying suitable limits of the shear and noise parameters. The crucial technical ingredient for making this approach rigorous is a result on the continuity of Lyapunov exponents via Furstenberg Khasminskii formulas.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDigital Object Identiﬁer (DOI) https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-023-04764-z (https://refubium.fu-berlin.de/bitstream/handle/fub188/39952/s00220-023-04764-z.pdf?isAllowed=y&save=y&sequence=2)\nciteturn7search13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 6 months ago; Positive Lyapunov Exponent in the Hopf Normal Form ... E-mail: dennis.chemnitz2@fu-berlin.de; maximilian.engel@fu-berlin.de\nDigital Object Identiﬁer (DOI) https://doi.org/10.1007/s00220-023-04764-z\nCommun. Math. Phys. 402, 1807–1843 (2023)\nCommunications in\nMathematical\nPhysics\nPositive Lyapunov Exponent in the Hopf Normal Form\nwith Additive Noise\nDennis Chemnitz\n, Maximilian Engel\nInstitut für Mathematik, Freie Universität Berlin, Arnimallee 6, 14195 Berlin, Germany.\nE-mail: dennis.chemnitz2@fu-berlin.de; maximilian.engel@fu-berlin.de\nReceived: 13 December 2022 / Accepted: 10 May 2023\nPublished online: 26 June 2023 – © The Author(s) 2023\nAbstract: We prove the positivity of Lyapunov exponents for the normal form of a Hopf\nbifurcation, perturbed by additive white noise, under sufﬁciently strong shear strength.\nThis completes a series of related results for simpliﬁed situations which we can exploit\nby studying suitable limits of the shear and noise parameters. The crucial technical\ningredient for making this approach rigorous is a result on the continuity of Lyapunov\nexponents via Furstenberg–Khasminskii formulas.\n1. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe Bass and Topological Stable Ranks of $H^\\infty_\\R(\\D)$ and $A_\\R(\\D)$ (https://arxiv.org/abs/0806.3109)\nciteturn7academia14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 18.4 years ago; Title: The Bass and Topological Stable Ranks of $H^\\infty_\\R(\\D)$ and $A_\\R(\\D)$ ... Sasane stating that the Bass stable rank of $A_\\R(\\D)$ is two and the topological stable rank of $A_\\R(\\D)$ is two, settling a conjecture by the second author.\nTitle: The Bass and Topological Stable Ranks of $H^\\infty_\\R(\\D)$ and $A_\\R(\\D)$\nAuthors: Raymond Mortini, Brett D. Wick\nDate: Wed Jun 18 23:45:27 2008\n\nIn this note we prove that the Bass stable rank of $H^\\infty_\\R(\\D)$ is two. This establishes the validity of a conjecture by S. Treil. We accomplish this in two different ways, one by giving a direct proof, and the other, by first showing that the topological stable rank of $H^\\infty_\\R(\\D)$ is two. We apply these results to give new proofs of results by R. Rupp and A. Sasane stating that the Bass stable rank of $A_\\R(\\D)$ is two and the topological stable rank of $A_\\R(\\D)$ is two, settling a conjecture by the second author. We also present a $\\bar\\partial$-free proof of the second author's characterization of the reducible pairs in $A_\\R(\\D)$.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTHE BASS AND TOPOLOGICAL STABLE RANKS OF (https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/document?doi=54c6f021203db00d8004f5a4b500b155af81b9fc&repid=rep1&type=pdf)\nciteturn